UID:lead-king-loop-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260913T000000Z
DTSTART:20260913T080000Z
DTEND:20260913T120000Z
SUMMARY:Lead King Loop
DESCRIPTION:A spectacular fall color run through the Elk Mountains featuring a 25K course through Lead King Basin past Crystal Mill and the historic Town of Crystal\, an 8-mile Quarry Climb along the Yule Marble Quarry Road\, and a 2.5K kids fun run. Includes custom event shirt\, post-race BBQ lunch\, beer (21+)\, and finisher medal. All proceeds benefit Marble Charter School.
LOCATION:TBD
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:run-rabbit-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260913T000000Z
DTSTART:20260918T090000Z
DTEND:20260918T130000Z
SUMMARY:Run Rabbit Run
DESCRIPTION:Run Rabbit Run offers a 14th Annual 100 Mile Race (Friday\, Sept 18\, limited to 450 entrants with Tortoise 9:00 AM start and Hare 1:00 PM start) and 19th Annual 50 Mile Race (Saturday\, Sept 19\, limited to 200 entrants\, 6:00 AM start). The 100 mile race features a $100\,000 total purse with $20\,000 to the men's and women's winners—the highest purse of any 100 mile race in the USA. Both races are on a challenging\, spectacular course in Steamboat Springs\, Colorado. Registration is currently full but a waitlist is available. The race is a charity event that has donated over $700\,000 to northern Colorado nonprofits since 2007.
LOCATION:Steamboat Ski Resort\, 2305 Mt Werner Cir\, Steamboat Springs\, CO 80487
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pikes-peak-ascent-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260913T000000Z
DTSTART:20260919T080000Z
DTEND:20260919T120000Z
SUMMARY:Pikes Peak Ascent & Marathon
DESCRIPTION:The Pikes Peak Marathon\, founded in 1956\, is the oldest continually held marathon in the United States. It takes runners from Manitou Springs\, Colorado\, to the summit of Pikes Peak at 14\,115 feet and back down for a total of 26.2 grueling mountain miles with approximately 7\,800 vertical feet of ascent. The sister race\, the Pikes Peak Ascent\, is a 13.3-mile climb to the summit. Both races take place September 19-20\, 2026.
LOCATION:441 Manitou Ave\, Suite 100\, Manitou Springs\, CO 80829
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
