UID:blue-sky-marathon-half-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260913T000000Z
DTSTART:20261017T080000Z
DTEND:20261017T120000Z
SUMMARY:Blue Sky Marathon & Half Marathon
DESCRIPTION:Trail running event taking place on trails between Horsetooth Mountain Park and Devil's Backbone Open Space. Marathon on Oct 17 (9-hour cutoff) and Half Marathon on Oct 18 (6-hour cutoff). Course features 100% dirt terrain with 90% singletrack\, elevation gain of 3\,500' (marathon) or 1\,800' (half marathon). Includes aid stations\, finisher awards\, race meal\, and generous cutoff times designed for both veteran and first-time trail runners.
LOCATION:Blue Sky Trailhead\, Horsetooth Mountain Park\, Fort Collins\, Colorado
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bobcat-trail-races-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260913T000000Z
DTSTART:20261017T070000Z
DTEND:20261017T110000Z
SUMMARY:Bobcat Trail Races
DESCRIPTION:Bobcat Trail Races feature one of Colorado Springs' best city parks\, Palmer Park. Runners will enjoy views of the city and Pikes Peak from the rocky bluffs. The event offers multiple distances (50K\, 25K\, 10K\, 5K) with challenging trail terrain ranging from technical single-track to rolling hills and rocky outcrops. Organized by Aravaipa Running.
LOCATION:Palmer Park\, 3650 Maizeland Rd\, Colorado Springs\, CO 80909
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:blue-sky-trail-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260913T000000Z
DTSTART:20261017T080000Z
DTEND:20261017T120000Z
SUMMARY:Blue Sky Trail Run
DESCRIPTION:Trail running event taking place on the trails between Horsetooth Mountain Park and Devil's Backbone Open Space. The Blue Sky courses offer a north-south tour of the easternmost hogbacks of Northern Colorado's Front Range mountains. 100% dirt course with 90% sweet Colorado singletrack. Terrain ranges from smooth dirt trail to technical rock gardens. Features fully stocked aid stations\, generous cut-offs (9 hours marathon / 6 hours half marathon)\, finisher awards\, and finish line meal.
LOCATION:Blue Sky Trailhead\, Horsetooth Mountain Park\, Fort Collins\, Colorado
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:weekend-at-burney-runwalkcrawl-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260913T000000Z
DTSTART:20261022T180000Z
DTEND:20261022T220000Z
SUMMARY:Weekend at Burney Run/Walk/Crawl
DESCRIPTION:Weekend at Burney Run/Walk/Crawl is a laid-back trail adventure featuring a 4.8-mile looped course through beautiful private property near Baum Lake. The course offers a 50/50 mix of flowy single-track and dirt service road with rolling hills\, approximately 370 ft elevation gain/loss per loop. Multiple race options available: 48-Hour Challenge (Oct 22-24)\, 24-Hour Challenge (Oct 23-24)\, 12-Hour\, 4.8-Mile Loop\, and Burro Race. Features aid station with hot food\, broth bar\, and snacks. Cash prize awarded for most miles run. Solo runners completing 100+ miles earn belt buckles; those completing 100 miles in 24 hours earn special ultra buckles. All participants completing one or more loops earn a medal.
LOCATION:22800 Guest Ranch Rd\, Cassel\, CA 96016
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:all-out-kooky-spooky-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260913T000000Z
DTSTART:20261101T090000Z
DTEND:20261101T130000Z
SUMMARY:All-Out Kooky-Spooky
DESCRIPTION:The 15th annual Kooky-Spooky Halloween race featuring 5K\, 10K\, and half marathon distances. Starting from Jefferson County's NAAC Stadium\, courses wind along scenic Ralston Creek Trail and by Arvada's Blunn Reservoir. Includes costume contest\, free parking\, on-course support\, virtual options\, and serves as an official BOLDERBoulder Qualifier. Benefits the Colorado National Kidney Foundation.
LOCATION:Jefferson County NAAC Stadium\, Golden\, CO 80403
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:colorado-24-hour-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260913T000000Z
DTSTART:20261107T080000Z
DTEND:20261107T120000Z
SUMMARY:Colorado 24 Hour Run
DESCRIPTION:A community-focused timed event held on a scenic 1-mile flat dirt loop at the Swift Ponds Campus. Runners can push their limits to see how far they can go in a set amount of time\, with a festive atmosphere and shared meals throughout the day and night.
LOCATION:4927 County Rd 36\, Fort Collins\, CO 80528
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kessel-run-ultra-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260913T000000Z
DTSTART:20261107T060000Z
DTEND:20261107T100000Z
SUMMARY:Kessel Run Ultra
DESCRIPTION:Trail ultramarathon event located in North Fruita Desert\, Colorado featuring world-class single track trails with sweeping views of the San Juan Mountains and Colorado National Monument. All distances begin on fast\, flowing singletrack and progress to steep terrain on the Zippity-Do-Da Trail. Course elevations range from 5\,030' to 5\,541'. Event includes aid stations\, finisher's medal\, custom race shirt\, bib\, and BOCO Technical Trucker hat.
LOCATION:18 Road Parking\, Fruita\, CO (GPS: 39.31093\, -108.70360)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
